.TH RX 1 "" "rx @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rx \- pull, stage, rebuild and clean up a NixOS system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rx
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B rx
\fBhelp\fR | \fBversion\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rx
runs the NixOS update cycle against a dotfiles repository: it pulls the
latest changes, optionally updates the flake inputs, stages the changes,
rebuilds the system with \fBnixos-rebuild switch\fR, deletes old generations
and optionally shows the closure diff.
.PP
Every external command runs via argv (no shell), and each step fails fast:
a failed pull, stage or rebuild aborts before the next step.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-repo " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to the dotfiles repository. Default: \fB~/.dotfiles\fR.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-hostname " " \fINAME\fR
Hostname used for the flake attribute (\fIPATH\fR#\fINAME\fR). Default:
detected from \fB/proc/sys/kernel/hostname\fR, \fB$HOSTNAME\fR or the
\fBhostname\fR command.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep " " \fIN\fR
Generations to keep during cleanup (1\-255). Default: \fB10\fR.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIN\fR
Cap \fBnix\fR \fB\-\-max\-jobs\fR for the rebuild (1\-65535).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cores " " \fIN\fR
Cap \fBnix\fR \fB\-\-cores\fR for the rebuild (1\-65535).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-update
Run \fBnix flake update\fR before staging.
.TP
.BI \-\-update\-command " " \fICOMMAND\fR
Replace \fBnix flake update\fR with \fICOMMAND\fR, run with the repository as
its working directory. Words are split on whitespace and run via argv: there is
no shell, so quotes are literal. Setting it also enables the update step,
unless \fB\-\-only\fR says otherwise.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-diff
Show the closure diff between the previous and current generation.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Assume yes for every prompt.
.TP
.BI \-\-only " " \fISTEPS\fR
Run only the listed comma-separated steps: \fBpull\fR, \fBflake\fR,
\fBstage\fR, \fBrebuild\fR, \fBcleanup\fR, \fBdiff\fR. \fBupdate\fR is accepted
as an alias for \fBflake\fR. The list wins over \fB\-\-update\fR and
\fB\-\-diff\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print each command instead of executing it. The read-only capability probe of
\fBnixos\-rebuild\fR still runs, so the preview shows the flavour actually
installed. Nothing else is executed: \fBsudo\fR is never invoked and no
credentials are cached.
.TP
.BI \-\-nom= \fITRUE\fR|\fIFALSE\fR
Pipe the rebuild's log through \fBnom\fR (nix\-output\-monitor) when it is
installed, which is the default. \fBtrue\fR insists on it.
The command keeps its stdin and stdout, so prompts still work; only the build
log (stderr) goes through the monitor. Pass \fBfalse\fR to run the rebuild with
its own output untouched. The flake package ships \fBnom\fR; other installs need
it on the \fBPATH\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-color= \fITRUE\fR|\fIFALSE\fR
Force ANSI colours (\fBtrue\fR) or plain output (\fBfalse\fR) on both streams.
The \fBCOLOR\fR environment variable takes the same values; without either, a
stream is coloured only when it is a terminal.
.TP
.BI \-\-completions " " \fISHELL\fR
Print the completion script for \fBbash\fR, \fBzsh\fR or \fBfish\fR and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the help banner.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH STEP SELECTION
Without \fB\-\-only\fR the pipeline is: \fBpull\fR, \fBflake\fR (only with
\fB\-\-update\fR), \fBstage\fR, \fBrebuild\fR, \fBcleanup\fR and \fBdiff\fR
(only with \fB\-\-diff\fR). Declining the staging prompt aborts before the
rebuild. A closed stdin is never treated as a confirmation.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or the user aborted at a prompt.
.TP
.B 1
A workflow step failed (pull, stage, rebuild, cleanup, diff).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments or configuration.
.TP
.B 141
Standard output was closed early (128 + SIGPIPE).
.PP
A child process killed by signal \fIN\fR yields \fB128\fR + \fIN\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.dotfiles
Default repository.
.TP
.I /nix/var/nix/profiles/system
System profile used for generation pruning and the closure diff.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nixos\-rebuild (8),
.BR nix (1),
.BR git (1)
